            <ArticleTitle>[Myofascial pain syndrome--fascial muscle pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1921-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Symptoms of myofascial pain syndrome, i.e. fascial muscle pain may occur in several areas of the body, particularly in the neck-shoulder region. The muscle pain symptom in the neck-shoulder region is commonly termed tension neck pain or nonspecific neck pain, but myofascial pain syndrome can also be distinguished into its own diagnosis. This review deals with the clinical picture of myofascial pain syndrome along with pathophysiological hypotheses and treatment options.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
